{#- The waitlist, as the landing ends on it, at the foot of a page that sells
    (2026-09-27). It took the place of "Keep what you learn" and its Sign in: a stranger
    who has read this far has no account to sign in to, and the door they can use is
    this one. Its own class rather than the landing's `part`, which `public.css` already
    means something by. -#}
<section class="front-join" id="join">
  <div class="split">
    <div class="part-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">{{ t("landing.page.the-waitlist", "The waitlist") }}</p>
      <h2>{{ t("landing.page.be-among-the-first-to-learn-hebrew-this", "Be among the first to learn Hebrew this way.") }}</h2>
      <p>{{ t("landing.page.we-re-opening-in-small-groups-leave-your", "We’re opening in small groups. Leave your email and we’ll tell you when it’s your turn.") }}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="join-card">
      {% include '_join_form.html.j2' %}
      <p class="join-note">{{ t("landing.page.free-to-start-with-the-whole-library-open", "Free to start, with the whole library open.") }}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
